## Part B: Collaboration Workflow Using Branching and Pull Requests

### Step 1: Create a New Feature Branch

Make sure you are inside the `Git-Practical-2` repository.

Execute:

```bash
git switch -c feature/update-readme
```

This creates and switches to a new branch named `feature/update-readme`.

### Step 2: Verify the Branch

```bash
git branch
```

The asterisk (*) indicates the currently active branch.

### Step 3: Edit README in the Feature Branch

```bash
notepad README.md
```

Add the following content:

```text
## Collaboration Workflow

This change is made using a separate feature branch.
Learning Git branching and collaborative development.
```

Save the file and close Notepad.

### Step 4: Check the Modified Files

```bash
git status
```

This displays the modified README file.

### Step 5: Stage the Changes

```bash
git add README.md
```

This adds the modified file to the staging area.

### Step 6: Commit the Changes

```bash
git commit -m "Updated README using feature branch"
```

This creates a commit containing the changes made in the feature branch.

### Step 7: Push the Feature Branch

```bash
git push -u origin feature/update-readme
```

This uploads the feature branch to GitHub.

### Step 8: Create a Pull Request

1. Open the GitHub repository.
2. Select Compare & Pull Request for the newly pushed branch.
3. Set the base branch to `main`.
4. Set the compare branch to `feature/update-readme`.
5. Enter the title: `Updated README using feature branch`.
6. Click Create Pull Request.

A Pull Request is created to request merging the feature branch into the main branch.

### Step 9: Review the Pull Request

Check the Files Changed section to verify the modifications.

GitHub displayed:
- No merge conflicts with the base branch.
- Changes can be merged automatically.

### Step 10: Merge the Pull Request

1. Click Merge Pull Request.
2. Click Confirm Merge.
3. Verify that GitHub displays Pull Request successfully merged and closed.

The feature branch changes are now integrated into the main branch.

### Step 11: Switch Back to Main Branch

Open Git Bash and execute:

```bash
git switch main
```

This switches the local repository to the main branch.

### Step 12: Synchronize the Local Repository

```bash
git pull origin main
```

This downloads and integrates the latest changes from the remote main branch into the local main branch.

### Step 13: Verify Repository Status

```bash
git status
```

Expected output:

```text
On branch main
Your branch is up to date with 'origin/main'.
nothing to commit, working tree clean
```

### Step 14: Verify Branches

```bash
git branch
```

